WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:04.104
This week we've been turning
the top of our show over t

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Late Night" writer
Amber Ruffin.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every evening,
she has told us stories

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
of her encounters
with the police.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.178 line:92%
Here once again is Amber.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The last two days,
I've told stories about

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.349 line:92%
my run-ins with the cops.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today I'm going to tell yo
a story about

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.286 size:84% position:42% line:92%
a run-in with the cops.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:26.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, I was living in Chicago,
and my friend Anthony

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.261 size:84% position:42% line:92%
had just left my house.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, he goes out the door,
across the porch,

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.602 size:88% position:44%
down the stairs, gets on
his bike and rides away.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:39.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
I shut the door, I go inside
I change into my pajamas.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.573 line:92%
And when I come out of my room

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
I see that
he has left his wallet.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I call him.
He comes back to get it.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:50.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
I step out onto the porch with
no shoes, in my pajamas.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
And instead of walking to
the end of the porch

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:55.221
and down the stairs, I jus
reach over the side of the porch

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.122 line:92%
to give him his wallet back.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:01:02.128
So, he rides up on his bicycle
and just lets his bicycle fall

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then reaches up
to get his wallet.

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, at that moment,
I'm reaching down

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:11.171
and he's reaching up, a cop ca
pulls up, flashes its lights

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:15.608
The cop gets out, and she'
like, "Hold it right there

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We gotcha!"

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, "Okay."

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.981 line:92%
Now, everything she says to us

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
she says with her hand
on her gun.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:29.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I'm terrified,
because while I'm a black lady

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:32.425 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Anthony is a black man,

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:37.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this cop is a tiny,
little white lady.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:40.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Now, I'm scared.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Anthony's scared.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:44.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had a lot of run-ins
with the cops at this point.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.473 line:92%
And isn't it hilarious tha

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:49.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
when people say
"run-ins with the cops,"

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
they mean they got caught
doing something?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:56.216
But when I say it, I just mean
being a person that they bother?

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.818 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Okay, so, this cop says,

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:02.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why were you guys
running from the police?"

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.556 line:92%
And we're like, "We're not

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not running anywhere.
I live here."

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.360 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And she's like, "Okay."

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile, I'm like,
bitch, I have no shoes on.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't say that.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say, "I'm in my pajamas
with no shoes on,"

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she goes,
"Let me see both your I.D.'s."

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.206 line:92%
I go, "Okay, but to get my I.D.,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to go
in the house, okay?"

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.210 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And she's like, "Fine."

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:28.781
So I go in the house, and
the whole time I'm in the house,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:32.085 size:75% position:38%
she's asking Anthony
a million questions.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I come up.
I give her my I.D.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.090
She says,
"This address is from Nebraska."

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And she's right.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:42.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Oh, yeah, I don't hav
a new Chicago I.D. yet."

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.698
And she goes, "Well, then I need
proof you live here.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Go get some mail."

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, this is where the story
takes a turn,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:52.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I can't describe it exactl
except to say

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:57.177
now she has unsnapped that thing
that holds your gun in place

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:00.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is holding on
to her gun tighter.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I go inside
and I'm freaking out

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she's going to shoot
my friend Anthony

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.854 line:92%
for just being bigger than her

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I go in,
and I tear up the house,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
looking for a piece of mai
with my name on it,

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I just moved there,
so I don't really have any

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:18.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I go, I get the mail,
I come out,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:23.603 size:75% position:38%
and for some reason,
she has calmed down.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.470 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I give her the mail.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
She looks at the mail, and she
looks at us and she goes,

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:31.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay, from now on, when I tel
you to stop, you stop."

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:36.049
Now, remember, she's never
told us to stop anything.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:36.883 line:92%
And I look at Anthony like

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.485
"Oh, my God, are you going t
handle this cop lying on us?

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:43.523
And he looks at me and he look
at the cop and he goes, "Okay.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.592 line:92%
I look at him and I go, "Okay,

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we live to get harasse
another day!

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:52.298
Because that's the kind of thing
you have to do

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.600 line:92%
to stay alive when you're black.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:04:00.740
You have to let the police
lie to you at your own house

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.508 line:92%
That's it. That's my story

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:06.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
We used to open this show
with fun jokes,

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.513 line:92%
but for the last three days,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:11.317 size:81% position:41%
we've opened this show
with stories about me

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.152 line:92%
getting mistreated by the cops

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:20.994
And if you're tired of hearing
these stories, do something!

